-From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
-Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 19:05:07 +0100
-Subject: [PATCH 21/46] VideoPlayer: keep a Blu-ray menu out of the subtitles'
- way
-
-The top menu of a Blu-ray 3D disc is invisible. The buttons are live -- enter
-starts the feature -- and moving between them brings the menu into view, where
-it then stays. Only the first drawing of it is lost.
-
-The navigator's menu goes into the same overlay container as the subtitles, and
-everything in there is treated as one sequence of cues. Three things follow from
-that, all of which the menu has to survive. Closing a subtitle stream empties
-the container, so opening one throws away a menu drawn moments earlier. A cue
-arriving with no stop time of its own is taken to end whatever came before it,
-so the first subtitle gives the menu a stop time in the past. And a forced cue
-supersedes an older forced one, which a menu is.
-
-Between subtitles all three are right; between a subtitle and a menu none of
-them are. So say where an overlay came from: CDVDOverlay carries a source, a
-subtitle stream unless told otherwise, and the navigator marks its pages as the
-menu. Ending and superseding then apply within a source and not across two, so
-the menu still goes when the next page replaces it or the navigator closes it
-with an empty one -- which is what takes it off the screen when a scene starts
-playing -- but a subtitle appearing over the top of it changes nothing. Closing
-a subtitle stream clears the subtitles and only the subtitles, so WebVTT cues
-behave exactly as they did. The menu is also marked unflushable, since a seek
-flushes the container and libbluray will not draw the page again on its own.
-
-libbluray composes a page only when something happens on the disc, so nothing
-would put a lost menu back, which is why moving a button was a way in.
-
-Seen on Gravity, whose menu playlist carries the PG streams that make Kodi open
-a subtitle stream over the top of the menu. A disc offering none of those never
-had the problem, which is why menus otherwise work.
-
-(cherry picked from commit a2948b86dca141762545e1b8dd310c99ef3d36a1)
